# The files of QEMU's data directory (share/qemu) that Beanjar's VMs load. share-trim.sh deletes
# everything else after `make install`, and fails if one of these is missing.
#
# One file per line, relative to share/qemu, then the QEMU targets (as in --target-list, without
# -softmmu) that need it; a file without targets is kept for every target. A comment above each
# entry says which device or option loads it.
#
# Measured with strace on webOS VMs: on aarch64 a VM booted to the Home screen and stopped, on
# x86_64 a q35 boot with the launcher's devices. The arm64 virt machine boots with -kernel, so no
# firmware (-bios, edk2, pflash), and its devices have no option ROM except the NIC's. QEMU's own
# descriptors (firmware/*.json), keymaps (VNC, curses and input-barrier only), trace-events-all
# (read by tracing scripts, not QEMU) and the other targets' firmware are not loaded; nor are VGA
# BIOSes, since the launcher's x86-64 VMs run with -vga none.

# virtio-net-pci's option ROM (its romfile property): QEMU refuses to create the device without
# it, whether or not the guest has firmware to run it
efi-virtio.rom

# q35's firmware, SeaBIOS: loaded as the machine's BIOS at every start
bios-256k.bin x86_64
# The option ROM through which SeaBIOS boots -kernel (with fw_cfg DMA)
linuxboot_dma.bin x86_64
# KVM's TPR-access patching ROM (kvm-apic), loaded under KVM; not opened under TCG, kept so a KVM
# start never lacks it
kvmvapic.bin x86_64
